  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Now the citric acid cycle, also called the Krebs cycle."
   ],
   [
    3.789,
    "It takes place in the mitochondrial matrix."
   ],
   [
    6.536,
    "Here the fuel derived from pyruvate is oxidized completely, and the cycle has eight steps, each run by its own specific enzyme."
   ],
   [
    15.208,
    "In step one, the two carbon acetyl group joins oxaloacetate, a four carbon molecule."
   ],
   [
    21.602,
    "Two plus four makes six: the product is citrate, the six carbon molecule that gives the cycle its name."
   ],
   [
    28.685,
    "Coenzyme A is released, free to pick up another acetyl group."
   ],
   [
    33.151,
    "The next seven steps rearrange and oxidize the molecule, step by step, until it becomes oxaloacetate again."
   ],
   [
    40.925,
    "That is why it is a cycle."
   ],
   [
    42.539,
    "The roundabout comes back to its starting point, and oxaloacetate is ready for the next acetyl group."
   ]
  ]
 },
