  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Let's walk around it once."
   ],
   [
    1.745,
    "In step two, citrate is rearranged into its isomer, isocitrate."
   ],
   [
    7.005,
    "In step three, isocitrate is oxidized, and N A D plus becomes N A D H."
   ],
   [
    14.076,
    "Then it loses a carbon dioxide."
   ],
   [
    16.302,
    "The molecule now has five carbons."
   ],
   [
    18.932,
    "In step four, another carbon dioxide leaves, and again N A D plus becomes N A D H."
   ],
   [
    25.781,
    "What remains is attached to coenzyme A, by a high energy bond, as succinyl co-A."
   ],
   [
    31.901,
    "Four carbons are left."
   ],
   [
    33.333,
    "In step five, that high energy bond pays for something."
   ],
   [
    36.927,
    "A phosphate group is passed to G D P, making G T P, and G T P can hand it on to make A T P."
   ],
   [
    44.453,
    "In step six, two hydrogens go to a different carrier, called F A D, making F A D H two."
   ],
   [
    51.992,
    "In step seven, water is added, and the bonds rearrange."
   ],
   [
    56.263,
    "In step eight, the molecule is oxidized, N A D plus becomes N A D H once more, and out comes oxaloacetate."
   ],
   [
    65.0,
    "You do not need to memorize the names."
   ],
   [
    67.357,
    "Just notice the pattern: carbon dioxide leaves twice, electrons are collected again and again, and one A T P is made."
   ]
  ]
 },
